# [OPT-5]/r48 F1: MULTI-CHAIN witnesses — patterns whose machines carry MORE
# scan-chain candidates than PCREC_MAX_SCAN_EDGES (4 per machine), so the
# selection cap's two sites (the pass's own conjunct, scanedge.c, and the
# emit-side annotation cap, emit_dfa.c) are both exercised with chains left
# OVER. Correct behavior either way the cap binds: unselected chains simply
# stay table-walked. Sabotage row S215 deletes the PASS-side conjunct and
# these cells are its detector. Expectations python3-re verified 2026-08-31.

# five counted single-class segments -> ~10 chain candidates across the
# forward machine ({m,n} splits at the accept transition), cap keeps 4
pattern [a-c]{2,4}[0-9]{2,4}[A-C]{2,4}[j-l]{2,4}[x-z]{2,4}
m "ab12ABjkxy" 0 10
m "abc123ABCjklxyz" 0 15
m "zzab12ABjkxyzz" 2 14
n "ab12ABjk"
n "ab12ABjkx"

# the unbounded-tail variant: four bounded chains + a * self-loop chain
pattern [a-c]{2,4}[0-9]{2,4}[A-C]{2,4}[j-l]{2,4}[x-z]*
m "ab12ABjk" 0 8
m "ab12ABjkxyz" 0 11
n "ab12AB"

# THE CAP-BINDING witness (S215's real detector; the two blocks above turned
# out NOT to bind the cap — their seam states carry two live classes, chains
# shatter, candidates never exceed 4 per machine; measured via the emitted
# 'scan edge:' comments, 2026-08-31). Literal separators make each counted
# segment a clean single-class chain: the REVERSE machine gets 5 candidates
# and emits exactly 4 (the cap binding), the forward machine refuses all of
# them (start-anywhere threading — the documented embedded refusal), the
# anchored machine binds too. Dropping the pass-side cap conjunct (S215)
# condemns the 5th chain's states with no loop to cover them.
pattern [a-c]{2,4}x[0-9]{2,4}y[A-C]{2,4}z[j-l]{2,4}w[x-z]{2,4}
m "abx12yABzjkwxy" 0 14
m "aabbx1234yAABBzjjkkwxxyy" 0 24
m "QQabx12yABzjkwxyQQ" 2 16
n "abx12yABzjkwx"
n "abx12yABzjkw"
